  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 26.0% a year from $4,319 million in FY2016 to $34,639 million in FY2025 [F1][F10][F231]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The path was a step change rather than a smooth climb: revenue rose 68.3% in FY2021 and 43.6% in FY2022, then fell 3.9% in FY2023 before recovering 13.7% and 34.3% [D258][D314][D370][D426][D483]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2022 jump included the Xilinx acquisition, which added Embedded revenue of $4.6 billion against $246 million in FY2021 [S110][S109][P41]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2023 decline came from a 25% fall in Client revenue on weak PC demand and inventory correction, partly offset by Embedded [P35]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2025 growth was driven by Data Center and Client and Gaming, with Data Center revenue up 32% to $16.6 billion [P15]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
